 "intro": "The gorge of the river Aous in Epirus, 198 BC, in the Second Macedonian War. King Philip V holds the pass. You are the consul Titus Quinctius Flamininus.",
 "debrief": "In Livy’s and Plutarch’s accounts, Flamininus was shown a path over the mountains by a shepherd sent by the Epirote chief Charops. A force of 4,000 men climbed it over three nights while Flamininus kept Philip busy in the gorge. When their smoke signal rose behind the Macedonian camp, he attacked from the front; caught between the two, Philip’s army fled, losing about 2,000 men. Flamininus then won over Greek cities with promises of freedom, and beat Philip at Cynoscephalae the next year. The other choices are what-ifs.",
